  "chair": {
    "_about": "The Sessellift quad chair made wider and hung lower (owner, LM2 and LM8): every point of the quad's chair (sessellift_fgq4.json chair) is moved by rule, nothing tuned by hand. Widths: a point's half-width grows by widen x t, where t runs from 0 at the hanger clamp (clampHalf) to 1 at the top bar's end (topBarHalf) and stays 1 beyond it, and widen = (seats - 4) / 2 x seatPitch, so the bench takes seats x seatPitch. Heights: every point under the hanger moves down by drop (the drawn chair hangs 3,238 mm from the rope to the bench's underside against the quad's 2,657; its top bar 1,737 against 1,160). The hanger is the drawing's: out of the detachable grip's arm, down and outboard round the station frame, and in level through the clamp. The grip is the Sessellift detachable grip (sessellift_detach_grip.json, LM10); the hanger starts at its socket under the arm. The bar gains a middle leg with a footrest, as drawn.",
